{
  "unit": {
    "id": "8",
    "title": "Yesterday I…",
    "blurb": "The past tense in every person",
    "intro": "The perfect tense tells what happened and is finished. Its endings are the same for every verb: -ī (I), -istī (you), -it (he/she), -imus (we), -istis (you all), -ērunt (they). The stem changes from verb to verb, so learn it with the verb: _edō → ēdī_, _videō → vīdī_, _veniō → vēnī_, _amō → amāvī_. Put a time word first and you have a story: _Herī pānem ēdī._"
  },
